# Code owners — who OWNS each surface. This file is documentation, not a merge gate.
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" is deliberately OFF on this repo, so no rule below can
# fire and nothing here blocks a merge on its own. The required approving review count is
# separately set to 0, for a related but distinct reason: a sole code owner cannot approve
# their own pull request, so any nonzero count would deadlock every merge.
#
# What main's protection actually enforces: a pull request is required, and force-push and
# deletion are blocked. That is the whole list. There are NO required status checks, and
# admin enforcement is off — so an owner with admin rights can push straight to main and
# bypass even the pull-request requirement.
#
# Merge-time checks are not mechanical here. ci.yml is workflow_dispatch-only
# (docs/decisions/0012-merge-time-local-ship-time-cloud.md), so the checks
# run on the machine making the change, from .pre-commit-config.yaml's pre-push stage. Those
# hooks must be installed per clone (`pre-commit install --hook-type pre-commit --hook-type
# pre-push`); a clone where that has not run has no automated gate at all.
#
# The one gate nothing local can skip is publish.yml's release-time job, which re-runs verify
# on Linux and Windows, the license check, and both Godot self-tests live, on the exact commit
# being shipped. Merging is discipline; shipping is enforced.
#
# So read the list below as "read this carefully before merging it yourself", not as an
# automatic stop. Sensitive surfaces = the places where tests can't save you (config, CI,
# secrets, self-executing code).

# Default owner for everything.
* @kphutt

# --- Sensitive paths: read carefully before merging ------------------------
# CI / automation / anything self-executing on a runner.
/.github/        @kphutt
/scripts/        @kphutt
# Toolchain + supply-chain surfaces.
/pyproject.toml  @kphutt
/uv.lock         @kphutt
/.gitleaks.toml  @kphutt

# --- Engine surfaces -------------------------------------------------------
# The mutation-operator catalog + the GDScript adapter are the tool's real
# technical risk (a wrong mutant = a silently wrong survivor report). Read every
# change here carefully before merging.
/gdmutant/engine/            @kphutt
/gdmutant/engine/operators/  @kphutt
/gdmutant/adapters/          @kphutt
/gdmutant/cli.py             @kphutt
